igned}u\\times v & =|u|\\cdot |v|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =7\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{117}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =49\\cdot (0.891\\,00…)\\cdot n \\\\  & =(43.659\\,31…)\\cdot n \\\\  & ≈43.7n.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278261 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "09aeb7f5-31e0-5b2d-9e2a-8eace54a6665" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product of Two Vectors Whose Angle Is a Non-Special Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6e75564-c905-5e49-8cc3-99c111eaf4d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.9n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278263} {:answer/id #uuid "534a220e-c103-57a1-a3df-2f8c92bd397a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15.8n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278264} {:answer/id #uuid "ed902961-0255-51ff-9616-7f07f2404175" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.8n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278265} {:answer/id #uuid "6ded683b-d1bf-5ca2-8d08-a1b611d06689" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.8n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278266} {:answer/id #uuid "68ebdef9-f6af-5ec9-ad45-862bbad148b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16.0n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "534a220e-c103-57a1-a3df-2f8c92bd397a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15.8n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278264} :answer-field/id #uuid "83be23a7-c30d-56f5-90d2-ca2a14367c66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278262}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3d7cc93e-bfe9-5037-a741-95d1d99bb730" :question/math-academy-id "q-1395" :question/problem "The vector $u$ has magnitude $8$, the vector $v$ has magnitude $2,$ the angle between $u$ and $v$ is ${100}^{∘}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $u\\times v.$ Find $u\\times v$ in terms of $n.$ Round your final answer to one decimal place where appropriate." :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|u|\\cdot |v|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =8\\cdot 2\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{100}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =16\\cdot (0.984\\,80…)\\cdot n \\\\  & =(15.756\\,92…)\\cdot n \\\\  & ≈15.8n.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278268 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82f31c6e-f9df-5e0a-88a4-a8ccfca00258" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product of Two Parallel Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c54e94d-2bca-5a7c-b6e9-e35241a6b451" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278270} {:answer/id #uuid "b6c7f087-a34d-54f8-9bbb-49cedd39134b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278271} {:answer/id #uuid "aa499afe-b5c9-579d-aa8e-72fe726de897" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278272} {:answer/id #uuid "b252661b-73d6-53d5-9f2a-131addd17d3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278273} {:answer/id #uuid "e3fc66c9-3c57-5596-8d33-cbe9648eedc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b252661b-73d6-53d5-9f2a-131addd17d3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278273} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c98495c-cd94-58bb-8685-e70162bd7668" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278269}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f9af397-1b9c-576f-9086-3715e41b26cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-146265" :question/problem "The vector $a$ has magnitude $5,$ the vector $b$ has magnitude $2,$ and $a∥b.$ Find $a\\times b.$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $a$ and $b$ are nonzero vectors. Then, $a\\times b=0$ if and only if $a∥b.$\n\nTherefore, $a\\times b=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278275 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82f31c6e-f9df-5e0a-88a4-a8ccfca00258" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product of Two Parallel Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ded8472-fc48-51fe-bf2b-6aaccc7b407a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278277} {:answer/id #uuid "c1660ef6-8741-5966-b26d-72008145561f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278278} {:answer/id #uuid "ae892eef-2dd5-545a-9088-fe9fa543ccec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278279} {:answer/id #uuid "96c7d8ce-69ba-5464-8827-17c9ad42553d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278280} {:answer/id #uuid "fc8313c1-b7ab-55d5-b2a8-2e5543cda634" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc8313c1-b7ab-55d5-b2a8-2e5543cda634" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278281} :answer-field/id #uuid "ceda88e7-1ba2-53cc-b05f-ddef2c392765" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278276}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "95994c1d-aad1-539b-89d6-72e8e47df0f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-146315" :question/problem "The vector $z$ has magnitude $2.$ What is $z\\times z?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $a$ and $b$ are nonzero vectors. Then, $a\\times b=0$ if and only if $a∥b.$\n\nNotice that any vector is parallel to itself. So, we have $z∥z.$\n\nTherefore, $z\\times z=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278282 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "09aeb7f5-31e0-5b2d-9e2a-8eace54a6665" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product of Two Vectors Whose Angle Is a Non-Special Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4290b716-920b-569f-adfe-371ad319240d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4290b716-920b-569f-adfe-371ad319240d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278284} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecd32614-5989-5e8d-8882-7411ba3951d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278283}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9dd60796-bafb-575a-a2e8-7433bc08aed6" :question/math-academy-id "q-279290" :question/problem "Given the vector $a$ has magnitude $8$, the vector $b$ has magnitude $2,$ the angle between $a$ and $b$ is ${172}^{∘}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $a\\times b.$ Find $a\\times b$ in terms of $n.$ \n\nType $n$ to represent the vector $n$ and round your final answer to the **nearest integer** where appropriate.\n\n$a\\times b≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|a|\\cdot |b|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =8\\cdot 2\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{172}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =16\\cdot (0.139\\,17…)\\cdot n \\\\  & =(2.226\\,76…)\\cdot n \\\\  & ≈2n.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
